# The committed scorecard is the one the README quotes. Everything else under reports/
# is regenerated by a run and should not be tracked.
reports/*
!reports/scorecard.md
!reports/conversation-eval.md
!reports/replay-baseline.json
!reports/load-report.html
!reports/load-report.json
!reports/fhir-check.json
# Held-out and rendered artifacts the docs quote. The sweep cannot be regenerated in CI at
# all (hours of provider calls), so committing its summary is the only way those numbers
# are checkable rather than merely asserted.
!reports/heldout-recall-none.json
!reports/heldout-recall-local.json
!reports/heldout-recall-none-s100.json
!reports/heldout-recall-local-s100.json
!reports/heldout-recall-local+llm-allam-2-7b-s100.json
!reports/canary-baseline.json
!reports/scorecard.png
reports-real/

